// Stories travellers tell, once they have decided you are not a danger.
//
// The opening line is not here — that comes from `content/openings.ron` and is
// drawn separately, so the same story does not always begin the same way.
//
// Rules a new one has to keep, all of them checked by tests:
//   * Three lines, none longer than will fit the dialogue box.
//   * At least two `needs`, each one a `need_id` in `content/passages.ron`.
//   * Never gender the speaker. The face is generated; the words do not get to
//     decide what it looks like.
//   * No greeting in the first line. They have already said hello.
//   * Places stay consistent with `docs/WORLD.md` — the Kiln in the north, the
//     Sill and drowned Sillford in the south, the company out of the west, the
//     rumoured terraces in the east.
//   * Nothing is remembered from before the ash. It happened a century back, past
//     anyone's grandparents; no traveller has seen the world work. Losses are
//     recent and personal.
//
// Which parties may tell which story is decided in `crates/game/src/visitors.rs`;
// a lone walker cannot tell the one about carrying a child out of a camp.
[
    (
        id: "mara_grief",
        traveler_name: "Mara",
        lines: [
            "My brother walked ahead to find the river crossing. Three days now, and no returning sign.",
            "I have gone back twice. The second time I could not tell my own footprints from the first.",
            "The road says to keep moving. My heart says I have left him behind.",
        ],
        needs: ["comfort", "presence"],
    ),
    (
        id: "oren_weariness",
        traveler_name: "Oren",
        lines: [
            "There are fever herbs in my pack for the settlement beyond the pass.",
            "Everyone called me strong when they loaded it. No one asked whether I was tired.",
            "If I rest, I fail them. If I do not, I may never reach them.",
        ],
        needs: ["rest", "courage"],
    ),
    (
        id: "fen_belonging",
        traveler_name: "Fen",
        lines: [
            "The north camp sent me away. They said there was not enough winter for another mouth.",
            "Perhaps a person can be extra, like a stone in a shoe.",
            "I do not need much. Only somewhere my name is not a burden.",
        ],
        needs: ["belonging", "mercy"],
    ),
    (
        id: "kell_toll",
        traveler_name: "Kell",
        lines: [
            "The men at the Kiln take a toll on the north road. I paid it going, and again coming back.",
            "The second time I had nothing left they wanted, so they took four days instead. Sitting.",
            "I am not ashamed of paying. I am ashamed of how quickly I offered.",
        ],
        needs: ["mercy", "comfort"],
    ),
    (
        id: "sarn_letter",
        traveler_name: "Sarn",
        lines: [
            "I am carrying a letter east, to a woman who does not know yet that her son is dead.",
            "I have had it eleven weeks. Every place I stop I ask, and every place it is not.",
            "I am walking as fast as I can towards the worst hour of somebody's life.",
        ],
        needs: ["courage", "comfort"],
    ),
    (
        id: "halden_water",
        traveler_name: "Halden",
        lines: [
            "A man asked me for water two days back, and I told him I had none to spare.",
            "There was a full skin under my coat while I said it. I have thought of nothing else since.",
            "I do not know what I am now. I would like to find out somewhere with a roof over it.",
        ],
        needs: ["mercy", "belonging"],
    ),
    (
        id: "ivy_column",
        traveler_name: "Ivy",
        lines: [
            "There is a company out of the west that used to be an army. It still marches like one.",
            "They came through our fields in the spring, and left the fields, and took everything that could walk.",
            "I go east because east is where the road goes. That is the whole of my plan.",
        ],
        needs: ["presence", "courage"],
    ),
    (
        id: "noa_pace",
        traveler_name: "Noa",
        lines: [
            "The last group I walked with decided one night that I ate more than I carried.",
            "They never did anything about it. They only said it where I could hear.",
            "So I keep my own pace now, and I am very tired of my own pace.",
        ],
        needs: ["belonging", "rest"],
    ),
    (
        id: "wren_seed",
        traveler_name: "Wren",
        lines: [
            "There is seed grain in this bag. It is not mine. It belongs to whoever ends up planting it.",
            "I have been hungry beside it nine days. It would feed me for two, and then it would be gone.",
            "Tell me I am right to keep walking. I have stopped being able to tell.",
        ],
        needs: ["courage", "rest"],
    ),
    (
        id: "ford_flood",
        traveler_name: "Ford",
        lines: [
            "The Sill came up in one night and took Sillford with it. I was on the high side of the water.",
            "Twice now somebody has told me I was lucky. I cannot work out what to do with being lucky.",
            "There were forty of us. I do not have a number for what there is now.",
        ],
        needs: ["comfort", "presence"],
    ),
    (
        id: "rilla_debt",
        traveler_name: "Rilla",
        lines: [
            "A family fed me through the cold months and asked nothing back. I left before the thaw.",
            "I could not stand being the one who only took. I thought going would settle it. It did not.",
            "If you feed me I will owe you as well, and I still will not know how to carry it.",
        ],
        needs: ["mercy", "belonging"],
    ),
    (
        id: "perrin_names",
        traveler_name: "Perrin",
        lines: [
            "I keep a list of names. People I met on the road who had nobody left to remember them.",
            "It is forty-one names. I read it through at night so that I do not lose any.",
            "Lately I have started being frightened of the day somebody has to add mine.",
        ],
        needs: ["presence", "belonging"],
    ),
    (
        id: "cass_ration",
        traveler_name: "Cass",
        lines: [
            "There is one meal left in our pack. It has been one meal left for three days.",
            "The little one thinks I already ate mine. I have got good at pretending to chew.",
            "I am not asking for me. I want to be clear about that before you decide anything.",
        ],
        needs: ["mercy", "rest"],
    ),
    (
        id: "rue_milestone",
        traveler_name: "Rue",
        lines: [
            "Our mother told us to wait by the milestone and that she would be back before dark.",
            "We waited two darks. Then the little one got cold, and I decided, and I have been deciding since.",
            "I do not know whether leaving that stone was the wrong thing. I cannot go back and ask.",
        ],
        needs: ["comfort", "courage"],
    ),
    (
        id: "elias_quiet",
        traveler_name: "Elias",
        lines: [
            "The little one talked all the time before. Not a word since the crossing.",
            "I answer things that were never asked, only so that there is a voice going.",
            "If something does get said while we are here, please do not make anything of it.",
        ],
        needs: ["comfort", "presence"],
    ),
    (
        id: "sela_offer",
        traveler_name: "Sela",
        lines: [
            "The camp below the Kiln takes children in. It does not take whoever brought them.",
            "They offered to keep the little one and not me. I stood there long enough to think it over.",
            "I want you to know that I thought it over. Then I picked the little one up and we left.",
        ],
        needs: ["belonging", "mercy"],
    ),
    (
        id: "amos_grown",
        traveler_name: "Amos",
        lines: [
            "Everywhere we stop, somebody works out which of us is in charge and speaks to me like a grown man.",
            "I let them. It is quicker than explaining, and we get given more.",
            "For one evening I would like to be spoken to as what I actually am.",
        ],
        needs: ["rest", "belonging"],
    ),
    (
        id: "bertram_stations",
        traveler_name: "Bertram",
        lines: [
            "I walked this road when there was a station on it every day's walk. Yours was the fourth.",
            "I can still give you the names of the keepers. Nobody has ever wanted them, but I have them.",
            "It is a strange grief, being the last one who remembers that a thing was ordinary.",
        ],
        needs: ["comfort", "belonging"],
    ),
    (
        id: "auda_knees",
        traveler_name: "Auda",
        lines: [
            "My knees have three or four more days in them. I have been telling myself six.",
            "There is somebody in the east I have not seen in nine years. That is all of the arithmetic.",
            "If I sit down I will not get up again, so I would rather stand while we talk.",
        ],
        needs: ["rest", "courage"],
    ),
    (
        id: "marrow_words",
        traveler_name: "Marrow",
        lines: [
            "I buried my wife on the ridge above the burnt orchard. Alone. There was nobody to send for.",
            "I said the words wrong. A hundred miles of going over them and I still cannot fix it.",
            "I did not expect to want somebody to have heard that. I have wanted it every day since.",
        ],
        needs: ["comfort", "presence"],
    ),
    (
        id: "hale_toll",
        traveler_name: "Hale",
        lines: [
            "I took a toll on this road once, for the men who are still up at the Kiln. Twelve years back.",
            "I left them. That is the only thing I have for the other side of the scale, and it is light.",
            "You should know it before you decide. I would rather be turned out than taken for better.",
        ],
        needs: ["mercy", "belonging"],
    ),
    (
        id: "corwin_terraces",
        traveler_name: "Corwin",
        lines: [
            "They say there is grain in the east. Standing water, terraces, a place that kept working.",
            "I have met four people who were told it and not one who has been.",
            "At my age it hardly matters whether it is true. It matters that I am walking towards it.",
        ],
        needs: ["courage", "presence"],
    ),
    (
        id: "tace_dog",
        traveler_name: "Tace",
        lines: [
            "I had a dog six years. She went off after something at the ford and did not come back.",
            "I waited a day and a half, whistling. I felt foolish, and I went on doing it.",
            "People tell me it was only a dog. They say it kindly, which is somehow worse.",
        ],
        needs: ["comfort", "mercy"],
    ),
]
